<newsitem itemid="154958" id="root" date="1996-10-30" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: J. Sainsbury H1 pretax profit slides.</title>
<headline>J. Sainsbury H1 pretax profit slides.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending September 21</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		14.36		  vs 16.99</p>
<p> Shr (pence)(diluted)   13.73		  vs 16.35</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.5		    vs 3.4</p>
<p> Pretax		     393		    vs 456</p>
<p> Turnover		   7,499		  vs 7,049</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 383 to 396 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 411		    vs 474</p>
<p> Interest		   36 payable	   vs 31 payable</p>
<p> Tax			  130		    vs 149</p>
<p> Net taxed		  263		    vs 307</p>
<p> Profit for the period  263		    vs 308</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 15, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  November 19</p>
<p> Ex-div date		November 11</p>
<p>NOTE - Supermarkets retailer J. Sainsbury Plc said profitability in the first half was held back by investments made to improve service and value for money in the second half of last year and by a price war on its petrol forecourts.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
